## Selector failure audit

- Pinned Java `DefaultMQProducerImpl.invokeMessageQueueSelector` and
  `sendSelectImpl` both catch selector `Throwable` and wrap it in
  `MQClientException`; its rendered message includes the standard FAQ suffix
  and retains the original cause.
- Added invoked Java coverage for both selector-only and synchronous send
  paths. `fixtures/producer/core.json` records each error class/message/cause,
  confirms one callback with a nonempty route, and has SHA-256
  `d1b05a04ed53dde2820647bd964ea2092592b35d51de90273f5b22f77ded0fe7`.
- Rust now catches unwinding selector panics, returns
  `ProducerError::SelectorPanicked` with the panic payload text, and renders
  the Java wrapper message. The scripted regression covers selector-only and
  sync send and proves both fail before Broker I/O. This closes only the
  thrown-selector slice; P18-V01 remains open.

